A||||6||Homicidal||Headlight motor cranks after I turn them off?||||8||
Z||000000||Homicidal||05-01-2000||12:45 AM||||It's just one thing after another, isn't it?<P>Right after replacing my clutch (1 day!) now my headlight motor is cranking after I turn them off!  This little black cylinder keeps spinning around and around and won't stop.<P>What is this thing, why is it not stopping and HOW do I STOP IT?  Help please!||||reg||8
Z||000001||TOM||05-01-2000||12:59 AM||||Stripped gear. contact rodney||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||05-01-2000||01:05 AM||||Yep, that's my guess too. Rodney Dickman sells them, but sometimes you can turn the little nylon gear 180 degrees and still use it since only half the gear is used.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Homicidal||05-01-2000||01:15 AM||||Anybody know any good instructions for removing the motor?  I would like to turn the gear around for the time being.<P>Right now I just left the headlights up, but I eventually want to fix this problem.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||05-01-2000||08:02 AM||||You did disconnect the single wire to get the motor to quit spinning didn't you?<BR>As far as removing motors, with the headlight up, loosen the 2 nuts on the bottom of the assembly, then remove the 2 at the top. then bring the headlight back down. You can use the knob or keeping fingers clear, hook up that wire with h/l switch off and light will go down.<BR>It iss a lttle fussy getting he assembly out, you'll probably donate some tissue and give blood, but such is the sacrifice. Once the assembly is out, itis pretty straghtforward to remove motor from assembly, 3 lon bolts hold motor to assm., 1 nut & bolt hold actuator arm to headlight.<BR>NOTE- there is a relay mounted to a bracket bolted on to te assembly. DON"T unbolt the bracket. The relay simply slides up and off.<P>As far as rebuilding the motors, someone else will need to help you there. I just replace mine with $20 pick-n-pull units.||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||05-01-2000||11:18 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/headlights.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/headlights.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||AL||05-01-2000||09:13 PM||||if i was you i would go to the junkyard and pull out the motorS off a trans am,first off the gears in the t a are not slanted at a angle like the fieros and they seem to last longer,if you do this take them apart and look at the gear it is different from yours, then clean out the oldgrease and clean the contacts, put in new grease and put them back together, but bEfore you do all this, when you pull them out of the t a remember tHat the left side of the t a motor goes on your right side and vice versa, so label them with a pen when you take them out, trust me they work better!good luck,AL. ||||reg||1
